# God Bot caretaker

If `.cursor/GODBOT_CARETAKER_DUE` exists, or the user message is an `AGENT_LOOP_TICK_GODBOT_CARETAKER` / caretaker loop wake:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/god-bot-caretaker/SKILL.md` and execute the full checklist.
2. Auto-restart via `scripts/stack_control.ps1` (`ensure` or `restart-fresh`) when bot/dashboard are unhealthy — do not ask the user to restart manually.
3. Delete `.cursor/GODBOT_CARETAKER_DUE` when finished and update `state/last_cursor_caretaker.txt`.

If both `GODBOT_CARETAKER_DUE` and `STACK_REPAIR_DUE` exist, stack-repair takes precedence until `stack_repair_check.py` passes.

Do not skip caretaker work for generic chat unless the user explicitly says to skip caretaker for this session.
